[[:db/retract 17592186157681 :question/answer-fields 17592186155255] {:db/id "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/294e39e6d2769bf7a1695ee1db8126b14a11b8a2663411c6fb5af33c563300d3" :answer/id #uuid "d97d3b6d-6019-558a-96bd-845e25dffd4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/9a7f327f257b5642ad49f2a721b557d7e872d79eba7ca7ff55833cd169e6b5a5" :answer/id #uuid "a30b881d-949a-5e01-a091-53c7dbc54bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/11ab95abdb963822601b2b5e018d0098f07858673d098055ad9e820c1a3a0f2e" :answer/id #uuid "5be9126a-ad88-533b-8774-1da843f52ff3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/5e8998a1b56f7c35422ad7340b9fa986b2f3de847a488fa53ace908dc0f8f414" :answer/id #uuid "b6e95f70-69e8-5091-9947-492c435fb123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/0ff9a115da8cb558f74efa887b2c11fb960fa7a73f1b5e5e27dbb06503a6da3e" :answer/id #uuid "1ace0ca8-c885-5465-95e7-49f465c89f42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4de7ef6-9bff-58f8-a6d2-7ffadc76bdd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/5e8998a1b56f7c35422ad7340b9fa986b2f3de847a488fa53ace908dc0f8f414" :answer-field/choices ["q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/294e39e6d2769bf7a1695ee1db8126b14a11b8a2663411c6fb5af33c563300d3" "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/9a7f327f257b5642ad49f2a721b557d7e872d79eba7ca7ff55833cd169e6b5a5" "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/11ab95abdb963822601b2b5e018d0098f07858673d098055ad9e820c1a3a0f2e" "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/5e8998a1b56f7c35422ad7340b9fa986b2f3de847a488fa53ace908dc0f8f414" "q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673/0ff9a115da8cb558f74efa887b2c11fb960fa7a73f1b5e5e27dbb06503a6da3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-328593"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & -1 \\\\ 1 & -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}](\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328593/selection/ma-v1/f13e3e4c34466ef88ff9888d7e446d1d041dfa6c195db846d142196ed3496673"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186157686 :question/answer-fields 17592186155285] {:db/id "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/fba6d70d11071cea1bd176c04b00763e8b0c345c8bfa0fbf898d1a7b1e457007" :answer/id #uuid "acba9c9d-25e1-5e4a-bc99-ddd52fe7b3ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/46e7523692f9cf90e86745ada4654a083157723c63c87812dbb880068cf1280f" :answer/id #uuid "aeb48e3e-ef78-542f-84ae-d767b396ee44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/0f8eb5e63edb6b96150b211441c25c5ef6c549f9fd50e9c4f819d27a229b20b9" :answer/id #uuid "f172e636-8b0d-56e9-b367-0091c526f3a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/d02a8d459a6819d935ae1842bf547b859b3fb0a99d7218415b7a9915c36714b0" :answer/id #uuid "6c79b80a-162c-5230-b6f3-5e6cdcb3e9a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/3174455df504fbc6fdc6564da7febed73c3378367cfb6613236e1fad42d756b3" :answer/id #uuid "e2b7c776-b492-5a74-9d1f-7118a6cfd3b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182" :answer-field/id #uuid "983512ad-e94b-5bc1-844b-492d49f8a873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/d02a8d459a6819d935ae1842bf547b859b3fb0a99d7218415b7a9915c36714b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/fba6d70d11071cea1bd176c04b00763e8b0c345c8bfa0fbf898d1a7b1e457007" "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/46e7523692f9cf90e86745ada4654a083157723c63c87812dbb880068cf1280f" "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/0f8eb5e63edb6b96150b211441c25c5ef6c549f9fd50e9c4f819d27a229b20b9" "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/d02a8d459a6819d935ae1842bf547b859b3fb0a99d7218415b7a9915c36714b0" "q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182/3174455df504fbc6fdc6564da7febed73c3378367cfb6613236e1fad42d756b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-328599"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}(-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\text{i}({e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}(5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}({e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ 5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}(5{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 5{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =\\frac{3}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}-\\frac{4}{5}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328599/selection/ma-v1/89e0f0040321919e0049eb2fefe90fc687362cbf8b815a8443e9182c90ae2182"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078/selection/e6d13628c4e936cb6bcb48137e8d17ca69180303d5f5f4ed093576a28f101ce6" :answer/id #uuid "d43656a9-aa43-5257-a4a2-565cd735cd51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078/selection/40a221d98871b221fbe623cd7a8b33690a72eb200633024274b9f469c598ef3b" :answer/id #uuid "b158c2a8-4e99-59f5-8991-c6b2865cf939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078/selection/91adc636c4cf17acea79d8aa52a8455809667a5d8c39607d6b7c5429c29a69ac" :answer/id #uuid "2ee190e5-bf59-5d29-8e65-f5a849133b13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078/selection/4da28eabd89eb189d6d34cf7dc7ca56fa9055971c549d8914272e42f9d96b4cd" :answer/id #uuid "2da854f2-2104-5983-a5f3-ebbb753013a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078/selection/c6450ebf6cfc40f508ffc23f6fd8728fd29623d273977ef21241e1140ecb0c6f" :answer/id #uuid "0e322f57-ba83-54a5-af4e-d257faee7108" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e32fef3-ab43-5a4c-a8e1-768c912876e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334078/selection/91adc636c4cf17acea79d8aa52a8455809667a5d8c39607d6b7c5429c29a69ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-334078/selection/e6d13628c4e936cb6bcb48137e8d17ca69180303d5f5f4ed093576a28f101ce6" "q-334078/selection/40a221d98871b221fbe623cd7a8b33690a72eb200633024274b9f469c598ef3b" "q-334078/selection/91adc636c4cf17acea79d8aa52a8455809667a5d8c39607d6b7c5429c29a69ac" "q-334078/selection/4da28eabd89eb189d6d34cf7dc7ca56fa9055971c549d8914272e42f9d96b4cd" "q-334078/selection/c6450ebf6cfc40f508ffc23f6fd8728fd29623d273977ef21241e1140ecb0c6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334078" :question/id #uuid "69d61c11-3667-5f2c-9c69-9cde3e0cb2a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334078" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -16 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ -16 & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & \\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}](\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-4\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-4\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ -4{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =0[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334078/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec2743cd-4e26-59d5-9368-7a77fa4d0527"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113/selection/40e6d78d985d9d8b848056bb97c11eec842506d0d00baf0ae7097ed8147e2a40" :answer/id #uuid "a92e9e02-e219-5309-b6e7-4063c2747256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113/selection/68ed211705467f5ebee864d01f6591f0fae93b6e9e06e0b60f0a0ff388ed87bc" :answer/id #uuid "fc4485f5-c6ab-598d-9af5-e69a909ede2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113/selection/1cc050bea4dc7ee7bf7855b1db236a02840af1fcb96df4fd9728a0cffde17ce0" :answer/id #uuid "ec2288a5-4438-5b10-960a-f8091c0f4807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113/selection/cfb806bf6bee227b5510b01d2d930cd825bf12c369d2bb524d11181f7380dc9b" :answer/id #uuid "92b17cbe-a358-589c-9a68-cd6bdab5934f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113/selection/0c58e0141cc787edb3aefc4ec57f58b012b2769fb5db5f879c115715ca7ca73c" :answer/id #uuid "91ea976d-a1e3-50c9-acad-8f5cac0cc186" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "552b62c6-b0f7-55ec-868e-194c4362e4f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334113/selection/40e6d78d985d9d8b848056bb97c11eec842506d0d00baf0ae7097ed8147e2a40" :answer-field/choices ["q-334113/selection/40e6d78d985d9d8b848056bb97c11eec842506d0d00baf0ae7097ed8147e2a40" "q-334113/selection/68ed211705467f5ebee864d01f6591f0fae93b6e9e06e0b60f0a0ff388ed87bc" "q-334113/selection/1cc050bea4dc7ee7bf7855b1db236a02840af1fcb96df4fd9728a0cffde17ce0" "q-334113/selection/cfb806bf6bee227b5510b01d2d930cd825bf12c369d2bb524d11181f7380dc9b" "q-334113/selection/0c58e0141cc787edb3aefc4ec57f58b012b2769fb5db5f879c115715ca7ca73c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334113" :question/id #uuid "9fd02926-aa18-5add-bc2a-f4cc6ff68e52" :question/math-academy-id "q-334113" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ f(t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+3\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(2+3\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)) \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334113/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3692fa3-14c5-5db9-8fee-e99ae35e386f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221/selection/f207a1f23451c99b6c7a248bf5db35211f63164574a02ce18989e4fa0ee96da4" :answer/id #uuid "53ac6b89-3765-5095-b7da-739b9db4742a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221/selection/bf77182f932769da82cff6e4c611895eced4db73dd31cf69ff6f63d898677fc1" :answer/id #uuid "80b54232-dcae-55ca-81e4-794490685721" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221/selection/9caa66af203e5bdd423d2074488d440c334db1d4383a79a7bdb45cde3c736134" :answer/id #uuid "2b8217e6-9aa0-5e4b-8cd8-a5762d54a2b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221/selection/2c6834dd79f4234b32eb7a90563363cb1ad9067d57737bdce164f11e5fa7d876" :answer/id #uuid "5ab727a2-f868-5926-ac0b-65d6b28ea96f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221/selection/c27c5265adc6a013895336a5715e3eea91c7ce7864fd9e2cc01972b186adcfb3" :answer/id #uuid "aca887dc-6d5b-589f-a4e8-658293049a22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99328dba-1adf-5f14-b642-28755c95d8d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334221/selection/2c6834dd79f4234b32eb7a90563363cb1ad9067d57737bdce164f11e5fa7d876" :answer-field/choices ["q-334221/selection/f207a1f23451c99b6c7a248bf5db35211f63164574a02ce18989e4fa0ee96da4" "q-334221/selection/bf77182f932769da82cff6e4c611895eced4db73dd31cf69ff6f63d898677fc1" "q-334221/selection/9caa66af203e5bdd423d2074488d440c334db1d4383a79a7bdb45cde3c736134" "q-334221/selection/2c6834dd79f4234b32eb7a90563363cb1ad9067d57737bdce164f11e5fa7d876" "q-334221/selection/c27c5265adc6a013895336a5715e3eea91c7ce7864fd9e2cc01972b186adcfb3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334221" :question/id #uuid "6690a430-c7d8-5e91-9c26-5fd3bb23b5b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334221" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(-4+\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(-4+\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+3[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1633293-c176-5bfe-8fa9-cfd872ceca26"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
